  "prompt": "Is the family home deductible from the gross estate, and up to how much?",
  "runtimeCommit": "1b36eeadb26d69f2b9ae28c8422afcc3fdd5c6d2",
  "answer": "### Short Answer\nYes, the family home is deductible from the gross estate, and the maximum amount deductible is P10,000,000.\n\n### Interpretation\n\n### Practical Meaning\nThe deduction for the family home can significantly lower the estate tax liability for the heirs. By allowing a deduction of up to P10,000,000, the law provides a financial relief mechanism for families, ensuring that a substantial portion of the family home’s value is not subject to taxation upon the death of the owner. This provision is particularly beneficial in preserving family assets during the estate settlement process.",
